{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI must ask you to stop worrying so. The letter from Immanuel, asking after my health, arrived with yours. I am quite well. It was merely a slight fever, the sort one often catches when changing climates, and it has already broken. I have been walking in the gardens here; the air is fresh, and my spirits are high.\n\nPlease do not let anxiety take hold of you or the boys. I am not a fragile thing to be handled with tweezers. I am still the same Hegel who walked into Napoleon’s camp at Jena. A little rest in Paris will do me more good than medicine. I shall take care of myself, as I always do, and return to Berlin when my work here is finished.\n\nWrite to me of the household, of the little ones, but keep your worries to yourself. I need your letters to be a comfort, not a report of distress.\n\nYours always,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795219269,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":206,"prompt_tokens":913,"total_tokens":1119,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-taXMQygZAryEBHIfImd4eBJVk75TAWO8","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":913,"prompt_ms":907.799,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.994303395399781,"prompt_per_second":1005.7292418255582,"predicted_n":206,"predicted_ms":4836.68,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.59356097560976,"predicted_per_second":42.38444552875113}}